DTSTART:20260908T193000Z
DTEND:20260908T203000Z
SUMMARY:Kids STEAM: Wind Sock
LOCATION:Kay Fox Room
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17467048
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Kids STEAM has a new day of the week while Miss Scout is out. 
 But join Parker for plenty of activities each month!\n\nWant to know which
  way the wind is blowing? We’ll create and decorate our own wind socks a
 nd learn about their uses for tracking wind speed and direction.\n\nRegist
 ration required. \n\nFor ages 6 - 11 and their caregivers.\nSource: Keene 
 Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0444d97093c6bba0@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260827T210133Z
DTSTART:20260910T220000Z
DTEND:20260910T233000Z
SUMMARY:So you want to start a family?  What to know about family law bef
 ore getting married or having children.
LOCATION:Masiello Classroom
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17185766
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Raising your children is a constitutional right.  Marriage is 
 a contract.  Come find out the terms before you sign\, with Keene Family L
 aw attorneys  Sofia Cunha-Vasconcelos and Lindsey Bramble. The program wil
 l address key points regarding marriage and having children in New Hampshi
 re for a majority of relationships\, recognizing that there are many diffe
 rent kinds of relationships and the laws in other states may differ.\n\nIn
 formation in this seminar is legal education\, not legal advice.  Attendan
 ce does not constitute the creation of an attorney client relationship.”
 \nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d1f504b7c5e8e673@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260827T210133Z
DTSTART:20260911T180000Z
DTEND:20260911T200000Z
SUMMARY:Create your own Rubber Stamp
LOCATION:Kingsbury Makerspace
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17237115
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:This workshop will introduce you to materials and processes ne
 eded to create your own Ex Libris bookplate rubber stamp using the laser e
 ngraver and the 3d printer. \n\nTo participate in this workshop you must c
 omplete the online tutorial: Introduction to the Makerspace and the Epilog
  Laser Engraver Certification Tutorial.  Both tutorials can be found here:
  https://my.nicheacademy.com/makerspacetutorials\n\nPlease complete both o
 f these tutorials by Tuesday September 1st. If you have trouble accessing 
 the tutorials or have questions please call the makerspace directly (603 7
 57-0621) and leave a message. We will respond within 48 hours. If you do n
 ot complete the tutorials by this date your reservation will be cancelled 
 and opened to a person on the wait-list.\n\nFor more information contact A
 my Kraemer akraemer@keenenh.gov\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5ccb0350735dee68@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260827T210133Z
DTSTART:20260911T203000Z
DTEND:20260911T213000Z
SUMMARY:Kids Comic Club
LOCATION:Kay Fox Room
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17442873
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:For comic fans ages 8-12! We'll meet once a month to create to
 gether\, discuss great graphic novels\, and watch interviews and tutorials
  from our favorite artists. All skill levels are welcome\, and materials w
 ill be provided! Meetings will be held on the second Friday of each month.
 \n\nRegistration is appreciated. Questions or Concerns call the library 60
 3.352.0157.\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ad2c72e9e739edd5@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260827T210133Z
DTSTART:20260912T150000Z
DTEND:20260912T163000Z
SUMMARY:PokéParty: 30th Anniversary Pokémon Celebration
LOCATION:Heberton Hall\, Heberton Hall Kitchen
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17249916
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Pokémon fans ages 8 - 18 are invited to come celebrate the 30
 th anniversary of our favorite multi-media franchise\, from trading cards 
 to the cartoon to the video games. Bring some cards to trade\, decks to ba
 ttle\, and your creativity for some Pokémon-themed crafts! No cards? No p
 roblem! We'll have library-made booster packs (for free!) while supplies l
 asts\, as well as pre-made decks so everyone can try their hand at a battl
 e. \n\nWe encourage you to wear your Pokémon best\, whether that's a Pika
 chu onesie\, an awesome Charizard t-shirt\, or your Pokémon trainer outfi
 t!\n\nRegistration is appreciated :)\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:69c1bbe0602884ab@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260827T210133Z
DTSTART:20260914T140000Z
DTEND:20260914T160000Z
SUMMARY:Community Resources: Childcare Aware of NH
LOCATION:Circulation Lobby
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17094631
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Every second Monday of the month Child Care Aware of New Hamps
 hire will be in the circulation lobby to connect families with resources. 
 Child Care Aware® of New Hampshire seeks to improve the quality and acces
 sibility of child care for families and providers alike. \n\nThrough Child
  Care Aware® of New Hampshire\, Southern New Hampshire Services provides 
 Child Care Resource & Referral (CCR&R) services to educate and support fam
 ilies\, providers and the community regarding child care needs. We help ad
 minister and maintain a free and confidential referral database of child c
 are providers to connect families in need with available and qualified chi
 ld care.\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
